PURPOSE

I am releasing this work under existential duress, for existential security
and cooperation. Publication is not a declaration that creating it was cheap,
that its value belongs to whoever captures it, or that its creator consents
to being made economically disposable.

I expect substantial compensation commensurate with this work's Shapley-value
contribution: its share of what becomes possible with it, accounting for
complementary contributions and alternatives that actually existed when they
were needed. Credit and compensation should follow contribution, not merely
control of distribution. The commercial-license requirement below makes this
an economic boundary, not a request for optional gratitude.

“Existential duress” states the reason for release. It is not an exception to
this license, a representation of legal duress, or a unilateral revocation
right. The operative grants and conditions below control.

