2. NO-FEE PERMISSION

Subject to this license, the Licensor grants a worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free permission to copy, use, modify, and redistribute the Work for:

(a) personal, non-commercial learning and experimentation;
(b) non-commercial teaching, scholarship, and research not primarily directed
    toward commercial product or service development;
(c) independent public-interest safety, security, accountability, or scientific
    scrutiny, including criticism of the Work and its Licensor; and
(d) narrowly necessary use to avert imminent death or serious physical harm.
    Such emergency use need not await a licensing negotiation. It does not
    authorize subsequent incorporation into an ordinary commercial service.

Safety scrutiny does not become commercial merely because its findings are
inconvenient, its researcher is employed, or its report receives ordinary
publication revenue. The exception does not cover using the Work as a
production component, commercial development tool, or commercial training
corpus under the label of a safety evaluation.

The permission covers applicable copyright and database rights held by the
Licensor, including extraction and reuse within the permitted purposes.
Patent and trademark rights are not granted. Compliant users' permission is
not revocable at the Licensor's discretion.

3. COMMERCIAL USE REQUIRES A SEPARATE PAID LICENSE

No commercial-use permission is granted by this public license. Before any
commercial use that requires rights in the Work, obtain a separate written
commercial license executed by you and the Licensor, and comply with its
payment and other terms. No agreement means no commercial permission.

Commercial use includes use primarily intended for commercial advantage or
monetary compensation, whether or not revenue has yet arrived. It includes
internal business operations; paid consulting or services; incorporation into
products, hosted services, or proprietary datasets; and using the Work to
develop, train, fine-tune, or operate commercial models or agents, subject to
Section 1's prior-rights and statutory-exception boundaries. Indirect use
through a contractor, affiliate, agent, or intermediary is not an exemption.
An organization's nonprofit status alone does not exempt its commercial use.
This paragraph does not narrow Section 2's permissions.

A donation, attribution, a valuation report, an unanswered request, or a
self-selected zero does not purchase commercial permission. A separate
agreement must expressly identify any fee waiver; none is implied here.
Negotiations do not authorize commercial use while they are pending.

